lied organizations on both sides view the race as settled.\n\nPrediction markets give Deluzio a 94 to 96 percent chance of winning, and no public general-election polls have been conducted. Headlines show Deluzio active on local issues, with a Bernie Sanders endorsement and speculation about a possible 2028 Senate primary run against John Fetterman raising his profile. Incumbency, financial dominance, and a favorable environment point to a comfortable Deluzio victory, with the main uncertainty being the absence of polling in the district.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9835, "margin": 15.12}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9786, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9791, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9758, "margin": 17.5}]}